cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Schwarzschild Black Hole Simulator"
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Real-time ray tracer for Schwarzschild black holes. Every pixel is a numerically
  integrated null geodesic (RK4, adaptive step); the accretion disk is rendered with a
  selectable Shakura-Sunyaev (1973) or Page-Thorne (1974) relativistic flux profile,
  relativistic Doppler beaming, gravitational redshift, blackbody colour and volumetric
  radiative transfer. Ships a sub-pixel shadow-radius probe that inverts the analytic
  value b_c*sqrt(1-r_s/r0)/r0 to within 0.13 % relative (0.11 px absolute), a
  reproducible companion paper with code-generated figures, and a double-clickable
  portable Windows build with NVIDIA GPU support.
authors:
  - alias: "AaronShawn"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AaronShawn/blackhole-simulator"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - black hole
  - general relativity
  - Schwarzschild metric
  - geodesic ray tracing
  - gravitational lensing
  - accretion disk
  - WebGL
  - three.js
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-09-13"
